   "etymology": "A formation in -s of Proto-Albanian *awa-deja, from earlier *dej, continuing Proto-Indo-European *dʰew-. Compare Old Church Slavonic давити (daviti, “suffocate”), Gothic 𐌰𐍆𐌳𐌰𐌿𐌹𐌸𐍃 (afdauiþs, “troubled”), Old Irish díth (“end, death”), Avestan 𐬛𐬎𐬎𐬀𐬌𐬛𐬍 (duuaidī, “we press”), Latin fūnus (“death”) and English die.",
